cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PiMorph in your research, please cite this software."
title: "PiMorph: typed endothelial junction graphs from microscopy"
abstract: >
  PiMorph is an open-source Python pipeline that reconstructs typed
  endothelial cell-cell junction graphs (pi-graphs) from fluorescence microscopy. It segments
  cell instances, infers conservative cell-cell contact graphs, extracts per-interface
  VE-cadherin features and morphology-state labels, and optionally quantifies Golgi-nucleus
  polarity. Validated on phase-contrast (LIVECell), H&E histology (NuInsSeg), specular
  microscopy (cornea), and HUVEC shear-stress imaging (S-BIAD1540).
